WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.210
At Aswan, in Egypt, a high
dam holds back the Nile,

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.070
forming Lake Nasser.

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.370
From there, the river flows
north, hundreds of kilometres,

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.970
to the sea.

5
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:17.510
Where it meets the sea, at Rosetta, a
5 kilometre seawall was built in 1991.

6
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.770
Why would a coast need a wall?

7
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:24.150
The Nile Delta holds more than
42 per cent of Egypt's people.

8
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.270
So how could a dam hundreds of kilometres
inland make a coastline vanish?

9
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:33.210
In this mission, you'll follow
the Nile from Aswan to the sea,

10
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.710
step by step.

11
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.510
Then you'll count what a crowded
delta loses when its shore retreats.

12
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: explain how a dam far
inland can make a coastline retreat.
